WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:01.700
One of the things that would be really useful
would be test people.

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:02.700
If you find swaths of the population that
have antibodies and have had the disease and

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:03.700
are presumably immune.

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:04.700
Those are people that could get back to work
earlier while other groups may maintain physical

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:05.700
distancing for a longer period of time.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:06.700
It's early to be talking about that, but we
need to start doing some antibody testing

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:07.700
of the population as soon as we have a test
that can be done in large numbers and it can

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:08.700
become part of the eventual plan.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:09.700
We're not there yet, but the eventual plan
of getting some parts of the population back

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:10.700
to work when it is deemed safe and appropriate
by medical professionals, not by politicians

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:11.700
trying to win reelection in a few months.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:12.700
I have a story today about true incompetence.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:13.700
Listen to this insanity.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:14.700
We just learned that last week a Trump administration
official called a Thai official and said,

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:15.700
hey, we need some PPE.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:16.700
What can you send us?

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:18.340
The Thai official said, wait a second.

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:22.960
You just sent us the same PPE you're now asking
us to send you.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.040
What on earth is going on here?

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:26.040
It's just one story.

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:32.200
It's a micro story, but it's really a microcosm
of the embarrassing, failed response of this

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:33.970
administration in dealing with the pandemic.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:35.740
We're having trouble getting masks.

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:37.840
We're having trouble getting gloves.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:41.730
Other PPE, personal protective equipment for
our medical professionals.

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:45.590
So a Trump administration says, hey, let's
call our friends in Thailand.

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:49.330
And says, hey, we need you to send us some
stuff like right away.

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:52.739
The Thai officials get confused and they say,
wait a second.

00:00:52.739 --> 00:00:57.170
Well, we just got a call from a different
person in your administration saying a plane

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:02.890
is bringing us that same stuff from you that
you are now asking us for.

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:05.990
Imagine the embarrassment and the confusion.

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:08.909
Our shipment to Thailand is en route.

00:01:08.909 --> 00:01:11.380
Well, we are asking them to send us the same
stuff.

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:16.159
The shipment was immediately put on hold so
that people could figure out to borrow a term

00:01:16.159 --> 00:01:17.549
from Donald Trump.

00:01:17.549 --> 00:01:19.799
What the hell is going on?

00:01:19.799 --> 00:01:25.179
Understand the level of incompetence and nonsense
going on here that you have the Trump administration

00:01:25.179 --> 00:01:29.990
sending stuff to Thailand and another part
of the Trump administration asking Thailand

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:31.649
for the same stuff back.

00:01:31.649 --> 00:01:36.439
We meanwhile, found out, as I told you earlier
this week, that the Trump administration also

00:01:36.439 --> 00:01:41.999
sent 18 tons of PPE to China in the first
week of February, while Trump was publicly

00:01:41.999 --> 00:01:46.470
downplaying the risk from the virus only to
now have shortages.

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:52.439
To be clear, the February 6th or 7th stuff
that went out was not from the stockpile,

00:01:52.439 --> 00:01:57.829
but it is still PPE that could have become
part of what was available to hospitals here.

00:01:57.829 --> 00:02:02.459
South Korea, meanwhile, had their first case
on the same day as the United States or within

00:02:02.459 --> 00:02:03.459
a few hours.

00:02:03.459 --> 00:02:08.209
Difference may have been a different day technically,
but within the same 24 hour period they had

00:02:08.209 --> 00:02:12.269
rolled out a test by February 7th when we
were sending stuff to China and pretending

00:02:12.269 --> 00:02:13.700
everything was fine.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:18.659
They had started contact tracing, fever clinics
and isolation.

00:02:18.659 --> 00:02:24.810
And still today, South Korea has fewer than
200 total deaths in the entire country of

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.489
51 million people.

00:02:26.489 --> 00:02:31.849
We had over a thousand deaths in a single
day multiple times this week.

00:02:31.849 --> 00:02:33.879
We are being led by the blind.

00:02:33.879 --> 00:02:36.599
This is a mess of a government reaction.

00:02:36.599 --> 00:02:39.709
And listen, you know, Trump has bankrupted
casinos.

00:02:39.709 --> 00:02:42.829
He's been in positions, were not a single
bank, would lend money to him.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:44.049
It's more of the same.

00:02:44.049 --> 00:02:50.980
Every day we have another disclosure about
gross, sustained, persistent incompetence

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:55.390
where Trump is publicly cheerleading his own
handling of the entire fiasco.

00:02:55.390 --> 00:02:58.859
While what's going on behind the scenes is
absolutely atrocious.

00:02:58.859 --> 00:03:03.790
When Mike Pence seems to have more of a clue
than you do, which is the case with Pence

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:08.170
and Trump, you know, you have absolutely no
idea what you're doing.

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:12.719
Check out the political article that reports
on this were linking to it on YouTube.

00:03:12.719 --> 00:03:18.370
And really, you know, you have to read it
to understand the dystopian nature of this

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:19.370
administration's failings.

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:25.159
And by the way, all of these missteps not
testing early, not mobilizing the stockpile

00:03:25.159 --> 00:03:30.400
of ventilators and other supplies early, not
coming up with a travel shutdown plan early,

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:31.480
